# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vercel's local link and pulled environment
.vercel

# Next writes this on every build from tsconfig; committing it causes conflicts for no benefit.
next-env.d.ts

# ── Environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `.env*` catches `.env.local`, which is where a real configuration goes. The negations below are
# LOAD-BEARING: in the repository this was extracted from, a bare `.env*` swallowed the documented
# template as well, so `.env.example` was never committed at all and a fresh clone had to
# reverse-engineer every variable from the source. Keep the negation whenever the rule changes.
.env*
!.env.example

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# GENERATED AT BUILD TIME by scripts/resolve-release.mjs, and deliberately not committed.
#
# It records whether a release exists right now. Committing it would freeze that answer into the
# repository and make it wrong the moment a release is published or deleted -- a second source of
# truth for the one fact the download button depends on, which is the mistake DownloadSection's
# header already argues against for checksums.
src/generated/
